# Agent start banner (mandatory — all projects)

Whenever **any** seat or Cursor **Task** sub-agent begins work on a ticket or PR,
announce it in **both** places **before** doing the work:

1. **Cursor chat** — first lines of that turn
2. **Tracker** — comment on the ticket: GitHub Issues/PR **or** Jira (per `tracker.provider`);
   also on the **PR** when work is PR-scoped (`github_issues`)

Use this exact heading shape:

```markdown
### <Seat> started
**Ticket:** <slug>#N   (or Jira KEY)
**Mode:** <short mode>
**Doing:** <one-line plan>
```

| Seat | Heading |
|------|---------|
| Hermes | `### Hermes started` |
| Athena | `### Athena started` |
| Hephaestus | `### Hephaestus started` |
| Themis | `### Themis started` |
| Argus | `### Argus started` |
| Other Task | `### <Name> started` |

**Helper (GitHub Issues / PRs):**

```bash
# GitHub Issues factories — issue number or pr:N
bash scripts/post_agent_started.sh <slug> <N|pr:N> <Seat> "<Mode>" "<Doing>"
# Jira factories — issue KEY (e.g. TST-123); requires projects/<slug>/.secrets/jira.env
bash scripts/post_agent_started.sh <slug> <JIRA_KEY> <Seat> "<Mode>" "<Doing>"
# Engine / explicit GitHub repo:
bash scripts/post_agent_started.sh --repo owner/repo pr:<N> <Seat> "<Mode>" "<Doing>"
```

`pickup_github_ticket` / `pickup_jira_ticket` already post `### Hephaestus started`
via the same helper (upsert — one living comment per seat+ticket).

**Tracker stacking (not a second comment):** GitHub/Jira cannot Slack-thread.
The helper keeps **one** `### <Seat> started` comment per seat+ticket for 6h:
identical Mode+Doing is skipped (Kairos K11); a new plan PATCHes and lists
prior starts under `Also started`. Override TTL with `AGENT_START_SESSION_TTL_MS`.

**Forbidden:** silent seat switches; implementing / reviewing / closing with no start banner;
status-only “working on it” without the `### … started` heading.

Applies to **every** factory slug (not only Pantheon). Product app rules may repeat this;
the engine rule is authoritative.
